  "field_mappings_approx": {
    "caveat": "APPROXIMATION: window aggregates (rep_exact_frac over w=10 windows) are NOT consecutive-chain detectors. OpenHands '4 identical action-observation pairs' and DSH repeat-tool-reminder [3,5,8] consecutive triggers operate on ordered step sequences; rep_exact_frac measures fraction of exact repeats anywhere in the window regardless of adjacency/order.",
    "openhands4": "OpenHands-style '4 identical action-observation pairs' \u2248 UPPER end of REP sweep (t=0.5-0.75; w=10 window with frac>=0.5 means >=5/10 repeats; maxrep>=4 subset n=121/143 is the closer analogue).",
    "dsh_358": "DSH [3,5,8] consecutive \u2248 sustained-high-REP region (t>=0.5, especially t=0.6-0.75; 8 consecutive in a 10-window forces frac>=0.7+).",
    "bias_direction": "Aggregates smooth bursts, so this sweep UNDERSTATES burst-guard precision / OVERSTATES its recall. Data-grounded support (assumption-backed, not proof): requiring BOTH frac>=0.5 AND maxrep>=4 (n=121, more consecutive-like) gives reader precision 0.421 vs frac>=0.5 alone 0.392, while discordant cells (frac-only n=22, maxrep-only n=22) each have stag rate 0.227 \u2014 i.e. the stricter consecutive-leaning conjunction is more precise at lower recall. corr(frac,maxrep)=0.903. Full step-level consecutive chains unavailable in this parquet, so exact burst-guard operating point cannot be measured here \u2014 stated as assumption + directional evidence, APPROXIMATION."
  },
  "consistency": "Sweep results point the SAME direction as frozen detector_families.json and gold_crosscheck.json. Families shipped-style repetition signals (exact_burst AUC 0.546, ngram_loop 0.530, openhands5 0.515) are near chance on step_wasted yet materially better on step_noop (exact_burst 0.677, ngram_loop 0.652, openhands5 0.663) \u2014 exactly what single-channel sweeps show: REP/QUIET separate objective/mechanical quietness well (REP>=0.5 prec 0.797 vs mech; QUIET>=0.5 prec 0.832 vs mech) but separate judged STAGNANT poorly (best recall-gated prec 0.516 QUIET>=0.9, 0.436 REP>=0.6; REP AUC judged 0.588 vs objective 0.834 in gold_crosscheck). Reader labels discount mere repetition/no-op (many high-REP windows judged PRODUCTIVE: 87/143 FP at REP>=0.5), while mechanical/objective targets reward it \u2014 consistent with STALL/NOV carrying judged signal (STALL AUC judged 0.688, NOV 0.679) and VER/WS failing (0.36). No contradiction found.",
